<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Internal Root CA – Installation Guide</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(145deg, #f0f4fa 0%, #e6edf4 100%);
            padding: 2rem;
            color: #1e2a3a;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1300px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
            backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
            border-radius: 2rem;
            box-shadow: 0 25px 45px -12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .download-banner {
            background: #0f2b3d;
            color: white;
            padding: 1.2rem 2rem;
            text-align: center;
            border-bottom: 3px solid #2c7da0;
        }
        .download-banner h2 {
            margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
            color: white;
            border-left: none;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }
        .download-btn {
            display: inline-block;
            background: #2c7da0;
            color: white;
            padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
            border-radius: 40px;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
            margin-top: 0.5rem;
            transition: 0.2s;
            border: 1px solid #61a5c2;
        }
        .download-btn:hover {
            background: #1f5e7e;
            transform: scale(1.02);
        }

        .tabs {
            display: flex;
            background: #ffffffcc;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
            padding: 0 1.5rem;
            gap: 0.25rem;
        }

        .tab-button {
            background: transparent;
            border: none;
            padding: 1rem 1.8rem;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #334155;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: 0.2s;
            border-radius: 1rem 1rem 0 0;
            margin-bottom: -1px;
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.6rem;
        }

        .tab-button:hover {
            background: #e9eef3;
            color: #0f172a;
        }

        .tab-button.active {
            background: #ffffff;
            color: #0f2b3d;
            border-bottom: 3px solid #2c7da0;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .tab-content {
            display: none;
            padding: 2rem 2rem 2.5rem 2rem;
            animation: fadeIn 0.25s ease;
        }

        .tab-content.active {
            display: block;
        }

        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(6px);}
            to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0);}
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 1.8rem;
            margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #0c4a6e;
            border-left: 6px solid #2c7da0;
            padding-left: 1rem;
        }

        h3 {
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            margin: 1.5rem 0 0.8rem 0;
            color: #1e4a6b;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        code {
            background: #1e293b;
            color: #e2e8f0;
            padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-family: 'Fira Code', 'Cascadia Code', monospace;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        pre {
            background: #0f172a;
            color: #e2e8f0;
            padding: 1rem;
            border-radius: 1rem;
            overflow-x: auto;
            margin: 1rem 0;
            font-family: 'Fira Code', monospace;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            line-height: 1.45;
        }

        pre code {
            background: none;
            padding: 0;
        }

        .note {
            background: #fef9e3;
            border-left: 4px solid #f3b33d;
            padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .warning {
            background: #fee2e2;
            border-left: 4px solid #dc2626;
            padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .success {
            background: #e0f2fe;
            border-left: 4px solid #0891b2;
            padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }

        .inline-code {
            background: #e9ecef;
            color: #b91c1c;
            padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
            border-radius: 6px;
            font-family: monospace;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        ul, ol {
            margin: 0.6rem 0 0.8rem 1.8rem;
        }

        li {
            margin: 0.3rem 0;
        }

        hr {
            margin: 1.2rem 0;
            border: 0;
            height: 1px;
            background: #cbd5e1;
        }

        @media (max-width: 680px) {
            body { padding: 1rem; }
            .tab-button { padding: 0.7rem 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
            .tab-content { padding: 1.2rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <div class="download-banner">
        <h2>📜 Internal Root CA Certificate</h2>
        <p>Download the PEM certificate to install it on your system using the guides below.</p>
        <a href="/rootCA.pem" download="rootCA.pem" class="download-btn">⬇️ Download rootCA.pem</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tabs">
        <button class="tab-button active" data-tab="windows">🪟 Windows (GUI & CMD)</button>
        <button class="tab-button" data-tab="debian">🐧 Debian / Ubuntu</button>
        <button class="tab-button" data-tab="rhel">🔴 RHEL / CentOS / Fedora</button>
    </div>

    <!-- Windows Tab -->
    <div id="windows" class="tab-content active">
        <h2>📁 Windows – Import Root CA (Force overwrite)</h2>
        <p>Use the <strong>Local Machine</strong> certificate store to trust the CA system‑wide. Administrator rights are mandatory.</p>

        <h3>📌 Method 1: Graphical interface (recommended)</h3>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Download the certificate</strong><br>
                Use the button above or open <code class="inline-code">http://ca.{{ k8s_host_domain | default('localdomain') }}/rootCA.pem</code> → save as <code class="inline-code">rootCA.crt</code> (rename extension to .crt).</li>
            <li><strong>Open Local Machine certificate store</strong><br>
                Press <code class="inline-code">Win + R</code>, type <code class="inline-code">certlm.msc</code> and press <strong>Enter</strong> (accept UAC).</li>
            <li><strong>Remove old certificate (force overwrite)</strong><br>
                Expand <code class="inline-code">Trusted Root Certification Authorities</code> → <code class="inline-code">Certificates</code>. Find your old root → right‑click → <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Import new certificate</strong><br>
                Right‑click <code class="inline-code">Trusted Root Certification Authorities</code> → <strong>All Tasks</strong> → <strong>Import</strong> → browse to <code class="inline-code">rootCA.crt</code> → next → verify store → finish.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="note">📘 Using <code class="inline-code">certlm.msc</code> ensures installation for <strong>all users</strong>. Avoid double‑clicking a .crt file (current user only).</div>

        <h3>🖥️ Method 2: PowerShell (as Administrator)</h3>
        <pre><code># Force overwrite root CA from HTTP
$url = "http://ca.{{ k8s_host_domain | default('localdomain') }}/rootCA.pem"
$storeLoc = "Cert:\LocalMachine\Root"
$tempPem = "$env:TEMP\rootCA_temp.pem"
$tempDer = "$env:TEMP\rootCA_temp.der"

Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -OutFile $tempPem
certutil -decode $tempPem $tempDer | Out-Null
$cert = New-Object System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates.X509Certificate2($tempDer)
$serial = $cert.GetSerialNumberString()

certutil -delstore Root $serial 2>$null
certutil -addstore Root $tempDer

Remove-Item $tempPem, $tempDer -Force
Write-Host "Root CA imported successfully" -ForegroundColor Green</code></pre>
        <div class="warning">⚠️ <strong>Admin required</strong>: Right‑click PowerShell → Run as Administrator.</div>

        <h3>🔒 Clearing HSTS settings</h3>
        <p>If you have previously accessed the internal domain over HTTPS, you must clear the HSTS cache after replacing the root CA.</p>

        <h4>For Chromium‑based browsers (Chrome, Edge, Brave, etc.)</h4>
        <ol>
            <li>Type <code class="inline-code">chrome://net-internals/#hsts</code> (or <code class="inline-code">edge://net-internals/#hsts</code>).</li>
            <li>In the <strong>Delete domain security policies</strong> section, enter your internal domain (e.g. <code class="inline-code">ca.{{ k8s_host_domain | default('localdomain') }}</code>) and click <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="success">✅ Restart your browser after these steps.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Debian / Ubuntu Tab -->
    <div id="debian" class="tab-content">
        <h2>🐧 Debian, Ubuntu, and derivatives</h2>
        <p>System‑wide trust store and browser-specific trust (Chrome/Chromium/Edge).</p>

        <h3>📥 1. System Trust Store</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y wget
sudo wget -O /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/rootCA.crt http://ca.{{ k8s_host_domain | default('localdomain') }}/rootCA.pem
sudo update-ca-certificates --fresh</code></pre>
        <div class="note">📌 Extension <strong>must be .crt</strong> for the system trust store to recognize it.</div>

        <h3>🌐 2. Browser Trust (Chrome/Chromium/Edge)</h3>
        <p>Chromium-based browsers on Linux use a separate NSS database. Run these commands to manually trust the CA:</p>
        <pre><code># Install NSS tools
sudo apt install -y libnss3-tools

# Add to the NSS database
certutil -d sql:$HOME/.pki/nssdb -A -t "CT,C,C" -n "K8s-New-Root" -i /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/rootCA.crt</code></pre>
        <div class="note">📘 This bypasses the need for <code>libnss3-tools</code> if performed via the browser GUI, but these commands provide the necessary CLI alternative.</div>

        <h3>🧪 3. Verification</h3>
        <pre><code># Verify system trust
openssl s_client -connect gitlab.{{ k8s_host_domain | default('localdomain') }}:443 -CAfile /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt </dev/null

# Verify browser database
certutil -d sql:$HOME/.pki/nssdb -L | grep "K8s-New-Root"</code></pre>
        <div class="success">✅ Restart your browser completely for the changes to take effect.</div>
    </div>

    <!-- RedHat / RHEL tab -->
    <div id="rhel" class="tab-content">
        <h2>🔴 RHEL, CentOS, Fedora, Rocky Linux, AlmaLinux</h2>
        <p>RedHat‑based distributions use <code>update-ca-trust</code> and <code>nss-tools</code>.</p>

        <h3>📥 1. System Trust Store</h3>
        <pre><code>sudo dnf install -y wget
sudo wget -O /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/rootCA.crt http://ca.{{ k8s_host_domain | default('localdomain') }}/rootCA.pem
sudo update-ca-trust extract</code></pre>
        <div class="warning">💡 To ensure a clean overwrite, remove the old bundle first:
            <pre><code>sudo rm -f /etc/pki/ca-trust/extracted/pem/tls-ca-bundle.pem
sudo update-ca-trust extract</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h3>🌐 2. Browser Trust (Chrome/Chromium/Edge)</h3>
        <p>Add the certificate to the Network Security Services (NSS) shared database:</p>
        <pre><code># Install NSS tools
sudo dnf install -y nss-tools

# Add to the NSS database
certutil -d sql:$HOME/.pki/nssdb -A -t "CT,C,C" -n "K8s-New-Root" -i /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/rootCA.crt</code></pre>
        <div class="note">📌 RedHat systems use <code>nss-tools</code> for the <code>certutil</code> command.</div>

        <h3>✔️ 3. Verification</h3>
        <pre><code># Check if certificate exists in the bundle
grep -i "Your CA Name" /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt

# Check browser database
certutil -d sql:$HOME/.pki/nssdb -L</code></pre>
        <div class="success">✅ Reboot or restart your browser to ensure all daemons pick up the new CA.</div>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    const tabs = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-button');
    const contents = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content');

    function activateTab(tabId) {
        contents.forEach(content => content.classList.remove('active'));
        const activeContent = document.getElementById(tabId);
        if (activeContent) activeContent.classList.add('active');

        tabs.forEach(btn => {
            btn.classList.remove('active');
            if (btn.getAttribute('data-tab') === tabId) btn.classList.add('active');
        });
        localStorage.setItem('lastRootCATab', tabId);
    }

    tabs.forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => activateTab(btn.getAttribute('data-tab')));
    });

    const lastTab = localStorage.getItem('lastRootCATab');
    if (lastTab && ['windows', 'debian', 'rhel'].includes(lastTab)) activateTab(lastTab);
</script>
</body>
</html>
